            "explanation": {
                "english": "Given mass m = 1 kg, L = 2.25 × 10^6 J/kg, P = 100 kPa = 10^5 N/m^2. \nHeat supplied Q = mL = 1 × 2.25 × 10^6 J = 2.25 × 10^6 J.\nVolume of 1 kg water V_1 = m / rho_water = 1 / 1000 = 0.001 m^3.\nVolume of 1 kg steam V_2 = m / rho_steam = 1 / 0.6 = 1.667 m^3.\nWork done W = P(V_2 - V_1) = 10^5 × (1.667 - 0.001) ≈ 10^5 × 1.666 = 1.666 × 10^5 J = 0.1666 × 10^6 J.\nIncrease in internal energy \\Delta U = Q - W = 2.25 × 10^6 - 0.167 × 10^6 = 2.083 × 10^6 J.",
